        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): block self-narrating auto-announce replies",
        "body": "## Summary\n- tighten cron auto-delivery instructions so automatic final answers must be the exact user-facing message, not a narration of what was sent\n- add a delivery-side guard that blocks compact self-narrating cron auto-announce text before it reaches outbound delivery\n- keep substantive user-facing messages and multi-line content deliverable\n\n## Testing\n- `./node_modules/.bin/vitest run src/cron/isolated-agent.helpers.test.ts src/cron/isolated-agent.direct-delivery-core-channels.test.ts`\n- Result: 2 files passed, 45 tests passed\n\n## Real behavior proof\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Cron auto-announce delivery should not send compact self-narrating final text such as a message that says the assistant already sent or asked the user something. It should block that internal/meta narration before outbound delivery and still allow substantive user-facing messages.\n- Real environment tested: Local OpenClaw checkout at this PR head on macOS, using the repository-installed dependencies and the actual cron isolated-agent delivery dispatch code path.\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: `./node_modules/.bin/vitest run src/cron/isolated-agent.helpers.test.ts src/cron/isolated-agent.direct-delivery-core-channels.test.ts`\n- Evidence after fix: Terminal capture from the local OpenClaw checkout after applying this patch:\n\n```text\nRUN  v4.1.7 /Users/jeremy-builder/Building/OpenClaw\n\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests  45 passed (45)\nDuration  5.20s\n```\n\n- Observed result after fix: The delivery regression exercises the cron direct-delivery path with a compact self-narrating final payload and observes `delivered === false`, `deliveryAttempted === true`, and no Telegram send call. The helper regression also observes that a substantive user-facing lunch-options style message is not flagged.\n- What was not tested: No live Telegram bot/group end-to-end run was performed for this PR; the proof is from the local OpenClaw runtime test harness and focused dispatch-path regression.\n",
